    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "First launched in 2001, the Le City tote is one of Balenciaga's most iconic designs. It was originally conceived as a cool, functional bag for girls to wear while riding motorcycles — hence its nickname, the 'Motorcycle Bag.' With no visible logo, its defining features include metal studs, leather pull-tabs, and a special washed-leather finish that gives it a rugged, androgynous look, challenging the prevailing aesthetic of elegance at the time.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "text": "Balenciaga Winter 24 campaign (swipe left/right for more images)",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Winter 25 collection welcomes a new member to the Le City family: the**Le City Moto**. Its clean, elongated baguette shape and soft leather naturally slouch, exuding an effortlessly relaxed attitude. The slightly upturned ends of the bag's opening complement two detachable straps.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
